TITLE='Registered title "The One Financial Trap Every Generation Fall" (as stored; grammatically incomplete, likely truncated or a typo for "Falls Into") is a single-secret frame with a generational hook. The script names the trap (lifestyle inflation) within the first two minutes and walks through each generation, so the promise is delivered.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White field. Left: the recurring cartoon man, palms out, alarmed. Right: black headline "EVERYONE FALLS FOR IT"; below, a rusty bear trap with dollar bills in it, a red X over it, and a black curved arrow pointing at it. At 320x180 the headline stays legible and the trap-with-cash reads clearly. The headline repeats the title idea without a numeric claim.'
SCRIPT='A single-narrator explainer framed by two composite brothers (Carter and Colton): hook, Goldman paycheck-to-paycheck statistic, definition of lifestyle inflation, a generational history (boomers, Gen X credit, millennials, Gen Z BNPL and social media), four psychological mechanisms (hedonic adaptation, social comparison, Diderot effect, present bias), compounding examples ($400 start-age, rent upgrade, subscriptions, raises), Millionaire Next Door and Buffett, experiences vs things, systems (Save More Tomorrow, friction, conscious spending, audits), and a callback close. Arithmetic reproduces; the 1980 credit figure is overstated and several survey numbers are unsourced.'
BEATS=['Hook: Carter and Colton, same start, different outcomes.','Goldman 41% paycheck-to-paycheck; lifestyle inflation defined.','Boomers: suburbs and home sizes.','Gen X: credit cards and HELOCs.','Millennials: two-income trap and the experience economy.','Gen Z: BNPL and social comparison.','Four mechanisms: hedonic adaptation, social comparison, Diderot, present bias.','Compounding: start age, rent, subscriptions, raises.','Millionaire Next Door, Buffett, Housel.','Experiences vs things; income and happiness.','Systems: Save More Tomorrow, friction, conscious spending, audit.','Callback and comment prompt.']
